"Usage: mentioned(<aforementioned>, <what>, <flag>, ...)";
"";
"Figures out which additional objects are mentioned when the flag <flag> is applied to <what>'s name.  'Mentioned' here means 'may require rephrasing when taken as the viewpoint.'.  Once those are figured out, they should be added to <aforementioned> and the lot returned.";
return args[1];

"Usage: for_pre(<context>, <what>, <flag>, ...)";
"";
"Figures out what kind of stuff will go in front of the name being modified when in the context <context>.  Returns a two-element list consisting of the updated context and some data to later be passed to for_post.";
return {args[1], 0};

"Usage: for_post(<context>, <name>, <pre_context>, <pre_data>, <what>, <flag>, ...)";
"";
"Does the actual in-context modification.  <pre_context> and <pre_data> are the updated context and data from when for_pre was called.  <context> is the current context.  Returns a list consisting of the updated context and modified name.";
return {args[1], `args[5]:("modname_" + args[6])(args[2], @args[7..$]) ! ANY => args[2]'};
